#EMBEDDED_NOTES
#Please note: This Procedure dataset uses animator shapes defined using the OSG file format and therefore will only animate using the CarSim VsVisualizer.
#
#In addition, this Procedure demonstrates the following CarSim features:
#
#(1) Target speed from path preview.
#
#(2) Defining a vehicle target path separate from the road geometry.
#
#(3) Using Events to define stop conditions as well as control the number of laps the vehicle makes.
#
#Target speed from path preview:
#The "Target speed from path preview" calculates a speed target over a preview distance to maintain the lateral and longitudinal acceleration with specified limits. Both the preview distance and acceleration limits can be defined by the user on the screen.
#
#When the speed target is calculated from a preview of the target path, the preview times for the driver-path follower are typically much shorter than for cases where the driver-path follower doesn't preview the path to obtain a target speed. For example, these preview times can be 0.1 - 0.15 seconds using path preview vs. 0.5 - 1.5 seconds for situations where the path preview is not considered.
#
#Since the target speed is very tightly tied to the exact path geometry, the path follower must be tied to it as well. As a result, "look ahead" distances are short.
#
#Handling course target path:
#The handling course target path is defined using a set of X-Y coordinates such as those that might be obtained from GPS or other instruments.
#
#Click on the 3D road dataset "Handling Course Target Path" for more information.
#END_EMBEDDED_NOTES

